{% doc %}
  The Cucuyo bug on a card: Cucuyo's own pieces carry it at the far end of
  the name's row, bottom-right of the card (Eugenia, 2026-09-29 — it replaced
  a CH monogram at the top-left, which ran into the transparent header on
  pages that open on a row of cards). Decided by the product's Vendor field
  and nothing else — no flag of its own to keep in step: Vendor "Cucuyo", in
  any capitalisation. Shared by the grid card and the curated card, and drawn
  inside their caption row (.card-caption), which places it.

  It takes the colour of the name next to it — the card's label colour, its
  Light tone, its hover colour — so it is not an <img> (an image keeps the
  brown it was drawn in): the drawing, assets/cucuyo-bug.svg as delivered,
  is the MASK of an element painted in currentColor (--cucuyo-bug, see
  snippets/css-variables). role="img" with the label a screen reader reads
  after the name: "Cheetah Pillow, Made by Cucuyo".

  @param {product} product
  @example
  {% render 'card-badge', product: product %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- assign vendor_key = product.vendor | downcase | strip -%}
{%- if vendor_key == 'cucuyo' -%}
  <span class="card-badge" role="img" aria-label="{{ 'products.made_by_cucuyo' | t }}"></span>
{%- endif -%}
